    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0931" n="903" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg903"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.5 MSP/11–1754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 395<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        the Republic of China</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-11-17T18:51:00-05:00">November 17, 1954—6:51
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. Department, FOA and Defense have two memoranda dated November 12 from
                    Chinese Embassy seeking additional military aid.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d395-f1"/>
                    First outlines Hsieh Plan which asks U.S. pay for (1) expansion facilities
                    accommodate 63,000 additional trainees at one time (50,000 Army, 7,000 Navy,
                    6,000 Air) plus all maintenance, administrative etc. expenses (2) clothing and
                    equipage for “the additional 341,700 men” (300,000 for Army, 26,000 Navy, 15,700
                    Air) (3) necessary expenses to fill up 20,700 vacancies in nine army divisions
                    to bring them to full strength. Total cost estimated US $106,225,000 and
                    itemized breakdown promised in due course. <hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi>
                    item “the additional 341,700 men” requires clarification.</p>
                <pb facs="0932" n="904" xml:id="pg904"/>
                <p>Second memorandum requests 4 destroyers, 6 destroyer escorts, 30 LST and 6 modern
                    non-magnetic minesweepers and gives justification need and planned uses.</p>
                <p>Assume you have similar proposals as indicated penultimate paragraph Section 3
                    your 340.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d395-f2"/> Coordinate with MAAG, FOA, Service
                    Attaches and cable joint comments soonest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d395-f1" n="1" xml:id="d395-f1-content">
                <p>The memoranda were sent to the Department as enclosures to a letter of Nov. 12
                    from Ambassador Koo to Secretary Dulles, filed as an attachment to a letter of
                    Dec. 14 from Robertson to H. Struve Hensel, Assistant Secretary of Defense for
                    International Security Affairs. (793.5 MSP/11–1254)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d395-f2" n="2" xml:id="d395-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 340 from Taipei, Nov. 11, commented on a tentative budget proposal for
                    the Mutual Security Assistance program for the Republic of China for fiscal
                    years 1955 and 1956. (794A.5 MSP/11–1154). The tentative budget figures had been
                    sent to Taipei in telegram 279, Nov. 3. (794A.5 MSP/11–354)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
